; onehotr_integer_model: ONEHOTR on an integer {0, 1, 2} model raises NonBinaryModel.
;
; ONEHOTR writes a one-hot penalty over grid row 0, and spec/xqvm/HLF.md derives
; every constraint expansion under x^2 = x, which fails for spin variables
; and for integer variables with k > 2. The check follows the declared domain
; (only a model allocated by BQMX passes), so spec/xqvm/ISA.md has ONEHOTR raise NonBinaryModel instead. Every other
; operand is valid, so the domain check alone decides.

PUSH 4
PUSH 3
XQMX r0          ; integer model, k = 3, 4 variables
PUSH 2           ; rows
PUSH 2           ; cols
RESIZE r0        ; 2x2 grid, so the grid precondition holds
PUSH 0           ; row
PUSH 1           ; penalty
ONEHOTR r0
HALT
